{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));s=json.load(open('../state.json'))\nfor col,identifier in [('claims','claim-notify-same-entry'),('bindings','binding-notify-completion'),('units','unit-claim-notify-same-entry')]:\n for x in s[col]:\n  if x['id']==identifier and x.get('version')==1: print(col,json.dumps(x,indent=2))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"claims {\n  \"id\": \"claim-notify-same-entry\",\n  \"kind\": \"obligation\",\n  \"concern\": \"implementation_semantics\",\n  \"description\": \"For an admitted append_notify operation, an Ok assigned position must identify that operation's proposed entry in the decided log; a different entry decided at that position under a later ballot must not satisfy the operation.\",\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"description\": \"Async runtime client completion within one valid fixed configuration, genuine non-Byzantine protocol/runtime messages, and successful storage. Focus on a delayed assignment across leader change when an old unchosen entry is replaced.\",\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Unique operation identity and distinct proposed values allow independent correlation.\",\n      \"No compaction obscures the compared entry.\",\n      \"Application transports actual messages to their intended recipients; delay and partition preserve per-directed-link FIFO among delivered messages.\"\n    ],\n    \"excluded\": [\n      \"No eventual-success or timing guarantee is imposed. Timeout, Superseded or a still-pending call is not itself a violation.\",\n      \"No claim of conflicting core decisions or persistent-storage failure.\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": {}\n  },\n  \"source\": \"Candidate derived from attributed implementation responsibilities\",\n  \"source_ids\": [\n    \"s-rt-api-contract\",\n    \"s-rt-wire\",\n    \"s-rt-error-contract\",\n    \"s-log-contract\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"assessment\": \"unassessed\",\n  \"candidate\": true,\n  \"grounding\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-rt-api-contract\",\n      \"s-rt-wire\",\n      \"s-rt-error-contract\",\n      \"s-log-contract\"\n    ],\n    \"expectation_ids\": [],\n    \"binding_ids\": [\n      \"binding-notify-completion\"\n    ],\n    \"derivation\": \"The public API promises to append an entry and await its decided log index. Wire identity associates the forwarded entry with the index actually assigned by the leader. Superseded documentation explicitly permits abandoning an uncertain operation after leadership change; it does not authorize successful completion for another entry. The obligation checks successful identity correspondence, not eventual commitment or mandatory supersession.\",\n    \"applicability\": \"A public append_notify operation and its actual completion within the same configured log; assignment produced by captured code and no compaction.\",\n    \"unresolved\": [],\n    \"conflicts\": [],\n    \"alternatives\": [\n      \"Success after leader change is permitted if the same proposed entry was adopted and decided.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nbindings {\n  \"associations\": [\n    {\n      \"claim_id\": \"claim-notify-same-entry\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-rt-api-contract\",\n        \"s-runtime-drain\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Public completion requirement is implemented by this result-producing function.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"anchor\": {\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-runtime-drain\"\n    ],\n    \"boundary_complete\": true,\n    \"kind\": \"declaration\",\n    \"material_id\": \"s-runtime-drain\",\n    \"start_line\": 201,\n    \"end_line\": 201,\n    \"symbol\": \"drain_notifiers\"\n  },\n  \"material_id\": \"s-runtime-drain\",\n  \"id\": \"binding-notify-completion\",\n  \"file\": \"omnipaxos_runtime/src/actor.rs\",\n  \"symbol\": \"drain_notifiers\",\n  \"start_line\": 201,\n  \"end_line\": 222,\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"d250f12902644004915d0c5133d5f7a9\",\n  \"content_digest\": \"1e4ee4f8d603a1b1407881807d1fff962e317eb80a735e589c9b15d907e24473\",\n  \"basis\": \"agent_inference\",\n  \"description\": \"Consumes assigned position and ballot to complete append_notify; success precedes supersession.\",\n  \"pending\": [],\n  \"excerpt\": \"    fn drain_notifiers(&mut self) {\\n        let decided = self.op.get_decided_idx();\\n        let now = Instant::now();\\n        let cur_ballot = self.op.get_promise();\\n        let old = std::mem::take(&mut self.pending);\\n        for p in old {\\n            match p.assigned {\\n                Some((idx, _)) if idx <= decided => {\\n                    let _ = p.reply.send(Ok(idx));\\n                }\\n                Some((idx, ballot)) if ballot < cur_ballot => {\\n                    let _ = p\\n                        .reply\\n                        .send(Err(AppendError::Superseded { log_entry_idx: idx }));\\n                }\\n                _ if now > p.deadline => {\\n                    let _ = p.reply.send(Err(AppendError::Timeout));\\n                }\\n                _ => self.pending.push_back(p),\\n            }\\n        }\\n    }\",\n  \"version\": 1\n}\nunits {\n  \"id\": \"unit-claim-notify-same-entry\",\n  \"candidate_id\": \"6852d4d265fa40f4a9fc812db9cbf110\",\n  \"obligation_ids\": [\n    \"claim-notify-same-entry\"\n  ],\n  \"binding_ids\": [\n    \"binding-notify-completion\"\n  ],\n  \"relation_ids\": [],\n  \"scope\": {\n    \"description\": \"Async runtime client completion within one valid fixed configuration, genuine non-Byzantine protocol/runtime messages, and successful storage. Focus on a delayed assignment across leader change when an old unchosen entry is replaced.\",\n    \"assumptions\": [\n      \"Unique operation identity and distinct proposed values allow independent correlation.\",\n      \"No compaction obscures the compared entry.\",\n      \"Application transports actual messages to their intended recipients; delay and partition preserve per-directed-link FIFO among delivered messages.\"\n    ],\n    \"excluded\": [\n      \"No eventual-success or timing guarantee is imposed. Timeout, Superseded or a still-pending call is not itself a violation.\",\n      \"No claim of conflicting core decisions or persistent-storage failure.\"\n    ],\n    \"parameters\": {}\n  },\n  \"rationale\": \"Ground the client completion responsibility and prepare a controlled schedule around a genuine delayed assignment; source analysis has not established a violation.\",\n  \"status\": \"partial\",\n  \"previous_id\": null,\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"boundary_changes\": [],\n  \"obligation_checks\": {\n    \"claim-notify-same-entry\": [\n      \"f6b6e1f52baa4f8991b6320420cee535\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"remaining_obligation_ids\": [\n    \"claim-notify-same-entry\"\n  ],\n  \"recheck_reasons\": [],\n  \"audit_question\": {\n    \"audit_spec_version\": 2,\n    \"disposition\": \"ready_for_check\",\n    \"preferred_check\": \"controlled_schedule\",\n    \"question\": \"Can append_notify return Ok for a proposal whose old-leader assignment arrives after a different entry has become decided at that assigned position?\",\n    \"importance\": \"False success can make an application acknowledge a write absent from the replicated decided log; the core consensus log could remain consistent while client completion is incorrect.\",\n    \"source_ids\": [\n      \"s-rt-api-contract\",\n      \"s-rt-error-contract\",\n      \"s-rt-assignment\",\n      \"s-rt-dispatch\",\n      \"s-runtime-drain\",\n      \"s-rt-loop\",\n      \"s-formation\",\n      \"s-rt-admission\",\n      \"s-rt-wire\",\n      \"s-runtime-pending\",\n      \"s-ble\",\n      \"s-ballot\",\n      \"s-api\",\n      \"s-lead\",\n      \"s-follow\",\n      \"s-support\",\n      \"s-append\",\n      \"s-storage-sync\",\n      \"s-sequence-quorum\",\n      \"s-storage-load-read\",\n      \"s-log-contract\",\n      \"s-reconfig-contract\"\n    ],\n    \"participants\": [\n      \"Origin follower actor\",\n      \"Old leader actor\",\n      \"New leader and quorum\"\n    ],\n    \"objects\": [\n      \"EntryId-tagged proposal\",\n      \"Assigned message\",\n      \"Decided entry at assigned prefix position\"\n    ],\n    \"contexts\": [\n      \"One configuration with stable identities, no compaction or crash\",\n      \"Old unchosen suffix excluded from new leader prepare quorum\",\n      \"Delayed genuine old leader message; per-link FIFO can be preserved\"\n    ],\n    \"event_paths\": [\n      \"Origin append_notify -> old leader TaggedProposal -> actual append -> delayed Assigned\",\n      \"New leader prepare quorum omitting old leader -> replacement append and decision -> origin receives genuine Assigned -> notification tick\"\n    ],\n    \"activity_classes\": [\n      \"A7\",\n      \"A1\",\n      \"A2\"\n    ],\n    \"behavior_ids\": [\n      \"b-rt-assignment\",\n      \"b-rt-notify\"\n    ],\n    \"fact_ids\": [\n      \"f-rt-assignment\"\n    ],\n    \"supporting_behavior_ids\": {\n      \"b-prepare\": \"New ballot selects history from a quorum excluding the old unchosen suffix.\",\n      \"b-decide\": \"Establishes the replacement decided prefix consumed by notification.\",\n      \"b-authority\": \"Changes origin promise before stale assignment arrives.\",\n      \"b-read\": \"Observes the actual decided entry for the returned assignment position.\"\n    },\n    \"obligation_relation_kind\": \"consumption\",\n    \"counterevidence\": [\n      \"EntryId prevents association with unrelated pending calls.\",\n      \"Batch reconciliation checks ballot equality.\",\n      \"Superseded is returned if assignment is already recorded and an intervening tick sees the new promise before the replacement is decided.\",\n      \"Existing supersession test waits for old call completion before replacement; it confirms that narrower guard path.\",\n      \"An old entry may legitimately survive a leadership change, so changed ballot alone is not a violation oracle.\"\n    ],\n    \"unknowns\": [\n      \"Clean execution must establish actual old entry acceptance, absence from new prepare quorum, replacement decision and late assignment for the same EntryId without forged messages or excluded FIFO constraints.\"\n    ],\n    \"priority\": 3,\n    \"trigger_rationale\": \"record_assignment admits an old real assignment by EntryId alone, while success checks position before ballot supersession. A fully assigned pending call is not necessary during authority transition. Source reading resolves guard ownership but cannot supply a legal executed history. This concrete identity/completion discriminator is more direct than the still-unclear cross-configuration routing contract; a controlled public-API check is justified.\"\n  },\n  \"coverage_limitations\": [\n    \"Bounded direct comparison completed; local attribution remains pending: Direct oracle correspondence is unreviewed\"\n  ]\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > make_review.py <<'PY'\nimport json\ns=dict(action='review',artifact_id='043c257412e64337a1b78ef10f7dcf2b',rationale='Review the actual completed identity comparison against claim-notify-same-entry version 1, fixed plan/harness version 1 and retained execution f6b6e1f52baa4f8991b6320420cee535; no executed inputs or predicates change.',review_items=[dict(aspect='checker_correspondence',status='no_issue_found',source_ids=['s-rt-api-contract','s-rt-error-contract','s-rt-wire','s-rt-assignment','s-rt-dispatch','s-runtime-drain','s-rt-loop','s-rt-lifecycle','s-rt-egress','s-rt-runtime-trait','s-rt-runtime-transport','s-config','s-api','s-follow','s-formation','s-storage-load-read','s-rt-test-superseded'],rationale='The accepted requirement is a successful append_notify result identifying its own proposed entry, not mandatory progress or mandatory Superseded. Public handle contract promises the entry\\\\'s decided index; Superseded documentation permits uncertain failure but does not permit success for another value. I reviewed the fixed plan and harness under direct-checks/8c4dc87dc3104a0ab63e5a71d28e1a3a and the stdout/stderr and parsed monitor record for f6b6e1f52baa4f8991b6320420cee535. Compilation and the real test completed. Setup asserts three unique configured nodes, leader 1 in Accept, empty accepted/decided logs and drained link queues. This occurs before the selected request, so it does not remove the investigated overlap. Core instances are moved into real actors. The only executor adapter delegates to tokio spawn/sleep through the documented AsyncRuntime extension point. The application owns transport; one FIFO per directed link is used in both prefix and fault phase. After setup, node 1 outbound messages cannot be delivered until explicit release of 1->2; no fabricated Assignments or modified protocol messages occur. Node 2\\\\'s actual tagged request reaches node 1 and produces an actual Assigned plus AcceptDecide containing 101. That old suffix cannot reach nodes 2 or 3 before their replacement decision, because every delivery uses the same link policy. The new leader is formed through public try_become_leader and real Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync interactions with nodes 2 and 3; large valid timeout configuration prevents irrelevant timer elections without replacing protocol logic. Events and outgoing channels are drained; setup asserts prerequisites rather than relying on process PASS.\\\\n\\\\nThe retained events correlate EntryId 43db97b7-53d4-47c6-a7b0-9cf04c2eb13a: admitted value 101; real assignment prefix length 1 in ballot number 1; old outbound delivered count 0 guaranteed by the single delivery policy; replacement Decided(202) at the origin in ballot number 2 while the target future is still pending; then the actual future returns Ok(1), and public read_decided_suffix(0) returns Decided(202). The fixed old_outbound_delivered field is a driver-policy invariant, not a separately sampled counter; inspection confirms all post-setup source-1 links are blocked until after replacement. The old acceptance diagnostic is derived from an emitted AcceptDecide inspected for value 101. The returned position is an accepted-prefix length, so k-1 is the corresponding zero-based index, matching append_tracked and core read classification. The measured value is read from the actual origin actor\\\\'s core storage through a public API, not inferred from the assignment or the proposed replacement. Stable op_id correlates the single target future independently of value; exact wire EntryId additionally links admission/assignment prerequisites and is asserted in the harness. No ambiguity or parse errors appear in the retained monitor record.\\\\n\\\\nThe implication requires observed_value == admitted.proposed only when the independently observed future result is successful. It therefore detects 202 \"'!= 101 without treating an error, pending call, timeout or changed ballot alone as a defect. Whole-link release preserves FIFO and delivers any preceding traffic; core old-ballot rejection can protect log consistency while the runtime consumes a stale assignment. Source ordering explains the observation: record_assignment matches EntryId without current-ballot validation; until receipt the origin has no assigned ballot to supersede; afterward drain_notifiers chooses index<=decided before comparing ballots. This source-supported cause is consistent with the real-producer endpoint witness. The semantic review finds no correspondence issue in this scoped comparison; controller assessment, not this label or process PASS, owns confirmation.'\"',report_title='旧任期分配消息导致写入被错误确认',report_answer='三节点同一配置中，101 的真实分配消息被延迟；新主节点随后在同一位置决定了 202。释放保持链路 FIFO 顺序的旧消息后，101 的 append_notify 返回 Ok(1)，但原节点读取到的是 Decided(202)。这验证的是客户端完成关联错误，不是两个节点决定了冲突日志。',counterevidence=['EntryId correlation blocks unrelated calls but does not bind the accepted position to the value occupying it after a new ballot.','The ballot-based Superseded branch works when assignment is already present and a tick observes changed promise before a replacement becomes decided; the captured repository test exercises that different schedule.','New leaders may legitimately adopt the old entry, so ballot change is insufficient for violation; this check directly observes a different value instead.'],limitations=['One fixed three-node history with batch size 1, MemoryStorage, no compaction or crashes and delayed genuine per-link FIFO traffic.','The endpoint is the original append_notify result and its origin\\\\'s decided log; no application database effects, conflicting core decisions, persistent-storage guarantees or exhaustive interleavings are claimed.','The existing historical preparation warnings in fixed metadata are answered by this compilation/execution; they are not evidence of another semantic problem.'])],feedback=dict(ref_ids=['6852d4d265fa4